From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: add KONKR Pocket FIT WSA2 sound card

The KONKR Pocket FIT shares the Pocket S2 WSA2-only speaker wiring.
Give it a board-specific compatible backed by the accepted channel mapping.

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,sm8250.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,sm8250.yaml
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@ properties:
           - const: qcom,sm8450-sndcard
       - enum:
           - ayaneo,pocket-s2-sndcard
+          - konkr,pocket-fit-sndcard
           - fairphone,fp4-sndcard
           - fairphone,fp5-sndcard
           - qcom,apq8096-sndcard
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -238,7 +238,9 @@
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(data->i2s_clk), "unable to get i2s clock\n");
 
 	data->wsa2_only = of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node,
-						  "ayaneo,pocket-s2-sndcard");
+						  "ayaneo,pocket-s2-sndcard") ||
+			  of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node,
+						  "konkr,pocket-fit-sndcard");
 	card->driver_name = of_device_get_match_data(dev);
 	sc8280xp_add_be_ops(card);
 	return devm_snd_soc_register_card(dev, card);
@@ -246,7 +248,8 @@
 
 static const struct of_device_id snd_sc8280xp_dt_match[] = {
 	{.compatible = "ayaneo,pocket-s2-sndcard", "ayaneo-ps2"},
+	{.compatible = "konkr,pocket-fit-sndcard", "sm8650"},
 	{.compatible = "qcom,eliza-sndcard", "eliza"},
 	{.compatible = "qcom,kaanapali-sndcard", "kaanapali"},
 	{.compatible = "qcom,qcm6490-idp-sndcard", "qcm6490"},
 	{.compatible = "qcom,qcs615-sndcard", "qcs615"},
